# Kong API Gateway URL.
#
# Proxy mode (default, leave empty):
#   Vite proxies /api/* to Kong :8443 (HTTPS/HTTP2) and /centrifugo-* to Kong
#   :8888 (HTTP/1.1 WS).  Bypasses system HTTP proxy (e.g. Clash on :7890).
#
# Direct mode (set to Kong HTTPS origin):
#   Browser talks straight to Kong — REST over HTTP/2 (absolute URL, no proxy
#   hop), WebSocket via WSS directly to Kong :8443 (no HTTP/1.1 downgrade).
#   CORS is already configured in Kong for https://localhost:3000.
#   Use this mode to mimic the production/browser-direct-to-Kong scenario or
#   to test concurrency without the HTTP/1.1 WS proxy bottleneck.
#
# Production build (served via nginx on port 22332):
#   Build with VITE_KONG_URL=https://localhost:8443 so the React app uses
#   absolute Kong URLs.  The UI runs at http://localhost:22332/ and calls
#   Kong at https://localhost:8443 (allowed by Kong's CORS config).
#
#   Example (dev direct): VITE_KONG_URL=https://localhost:8443
#   Example (prod build):  VITE_KONG_URL=https://localhost:8443
#   Example (remote prod): VITE_KONG_URL=https://your-server
VITE_KONG_URL=
